/ A file that isn't there is the NotFound error — delete has no option for it; the step's clause ignores it.
Start
- file.delete(Path="never-there.txt"); on.error(Key="NotFound", Recovery=[goal.call(Name="Caught")])
- assert.equals(Expected="NotFound", Actual=%caught%, Message="a missing file is NotFound")
- file.delete(Path="never-there.txt"); on.error(Key="NotFound", Ignore=true)
- variable.set(Name=%after%, Value="went on")
- assert.equals(Expected="went on", Actual=%after%, Message="on error 'NotFound' ignore carries on")

Caught
- variable.set(Name=%caught%, Value=%!error.Key%)
